Q: Winform loading WebUrl not determine whether is Browser or WinForm A: <p>I think that what you want to do is to have a webforms page that can detect the client's user agent.</p>
<p>One way you can do this is by modifying the <strong>User Agent</strong> string sent either by the <code>Microsoft.Web.WebView2</code> control (winforms app) or the browser.</p>
<pre><code>public partial class MainPage : ContentPage
{ 
    public MainPage()
    {
        InitializeComponent();
        LoadWebPageAsync();
    }        

    private async void LoadWebPageAsync()
    {
        // webView21 is the WebView2 control
        await webView21.EnsureCoreWebView2Async(null);

        string userAgent = webView21.CoreWebView2.Settings.UserAgent;

        // Modify the default user agent to let the 
        // web app distinguish between the browser(s) and
        // the winforms app
        webView21.CoreWebView2.Settings.UserAgent = $&quot;{userAgent} MyWinFormsApp&quot;;

        webView21.Source = new Uri(&quot;https://testmywebformpage.com&quot;);
    }
}
</code></pre>
<p>In your webforms app, the helper class becomes:</p>
<pre><code>public static class UserAgentHelper
{
    public static bool IsWinForms =&gt; HttpContext.Current
        .Request.UserAgent.Contains(&quot;MyWinFormsApp&quot;);

    public static bool IsWeb =&gt; !IsWinForms;
}
</code></pre>
<p>You can now check who loads the web app:</p>
<pre><code>if (UserAgentHelper.IsWinForms)
{
    Response.Write(&quot;Loaded on Windows Form App&quot;);
}
else
{
    Response.Write(&quot;Loaded on browser&quot;);
}
</code></pre>
<p>If you load the webforms app from within your winforms app you should see:
<a href="https://i.sstatic.net/G9nILOQE.png" rel="nofollow noreferrer"><img src="https://i.sstatic.net/G9nILOQE.png" alt="enter image description here" /></a></p>

Q: How do I use mongoDB driver with C++ in Visual Studio 2022 vcpkg A: <pre><code>🧰 1. Install vcpkg (if not already)
git clone https://github.com/microsoft/vcpkg
cd vcpkg
bootstrap-vcpkg.bat
📦 2. Install MongoDB C++ Driver

Use vcpkg to install mongocxx (the official C++ driver from MongoDB Inc.):

vcpkg install mongo-cxx-driver:x64-windows
🔗 3. Integrate vcpkg with Visual Studio
vcpkg integrate install

This makes Visual Studio 2022 automatically detect installed libraries.

🏗️ 4. Create a Visual Studio Project
Open Microsoft Visual Studio 2022
Create a Console App (C++)
Make sure platform = x64
⚙️ 5. Include Headers in Your Code
#include &lt;iostream&gt;
#include &lt;mongocxx/client.hpp&gt;
#include &lt;mongocxx/instance.hpp&gt;
#include &lt;mongocxx/uri.hpp&gt;

int main() {
    mongocxx::instance instance{}; // Required once per program
    mongocxx::client client{ mongocxx::uri{} };

    auto db = client[&quot;test&quot;];
    auto collection = db[&quot;mycollection&quot;];

    std::cout &lt;&lt; &quot;Connected to MongoDB!&quot; &lt;&lt; std::endl;

    return 0;
}
▶️ 6. Build &amp; Run
Press Ctrl + F5
If everything is set correctly → it will run without errors
</code></pre>

